      <SupplementalInformationDetail>
        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>PART X, LINE 2:</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>INCOME TAXES NECA/IBEW DRUG-FREE WORKFORCE PROGRAM TRUST QUALIFIES UNDER SECTION 501(C)(9) OF THE INTERNAL REVENUE CODE AND IS THEREFORE NOT SUBJECT TO ANY FEDERAL OR STATE INCOME TAXES. THE TRUST ESTABLISHED UNDER THE PLAN TO HOLD THE PLAN'S ASSETS OBTAINED ITS DETERMINATION LETTER ON FEBRUARY 28, 2005, IN WHICH THE INTERNAL REVENUE SERVICE STATED THAT THE PLAN AS THEN DESIGNED, WAS IN COMPLIANCE WITH THE APPLICABLE REQUIREMENTS OF THE INTERNAL REVENUE CODE. THE PLAN HAS BEEN AMENDED SINCE RECEIVING THIS LETTER, HOWEVER, THE PLAN ADMINISTRATOR AND THE PLAN'S TAX COUNSEL BELIEVE THAT THE PLAN IS CURRENTLY DESIGNED AND BEING OPERATED IN COMPLIANCE WITH THE APPLICABLE REQUIREMENTS OF THE INTERNAL REVENUE CODE. THE PLAN ACCOUNTS FOR UNCERTAIN TAX POSITIONS IN ACCORDANCE WITH FINANCIAL ACCOUNTING STANDARDS BOARD ("FASB") ACCOUNTING STANDARDS CODIFICATION, INCOME TAXES ("ASC 740"). THIS ADDRESSES THE DETERMINATION OF WHETHER TAX BENEFITS CLAIMED OR EXPECTED TO BE CLAIMED ON A TAX RETURN SHOULD BE RECORDED IN THE FINANCIAL STATEMENTS. UNDER ASC 740, THE PLAN MAY RECOGNIZE THE TAX BENEFIT FROM AN UNCERTAIN TAX POSITION ONLY IF IT IS MORE LIKELY THAN NOT THAT THE TAX POSITION WILL BE SUSTAINED ON EXAMINATION BY THE TAXING AUTHORITIES, BASED ON THE TECHNICAL MERITS OF THE POSITION. THE TAX BENEFITS RECOGNIZED IN THE FINANCIAL STATEMENTS FROM SUCH A POSITION SHOULD BE MEASURED BASED ON THE LARGEST BENEFIT THAT HAS A GREATER THAN FIFTY PERCENT LIKELIHOOD OF BEING REALIZED UPON ULTIMATE SETTLEMENT. THE PLAN ADMINISTRATOR HAS ANALYZED THE TAX POSITIONS TAKEN BY THE PLAN, AND HAS CONCLUDED THAT AS OF SEPTEMBER 30, 2024 AND 2023, THERE ARE NO UNCERTAIN POSITIONS TAKEN OR EXPECTED TO BE TAKEN THAT WOULD REQUIRE RECOGNITION OF A LIABILITY (OR ASSET) OR DISCLOSURE IN THE FINANCIAL STATEMENTS. THE PLAN IS SUBJECT TO ROUTINE AUDITS BY TAXING JURISDICTIONS; HOWEVER, THERE ARE CURRENTLY NO AUDITS FOR ANY TAX PERIODS IN PROGRESS. THE PLAN IS NO LONGER SUBJECT TO ANY SIGNIFICANT INCOME TAX EXAMINATIONS BY TAX AUTHORITIES FOR THE YEARS ENDED BEFORE SEPTEMBER 30, 2021</ExplanationTxt>
      </SupplementalInformationDetail>
    </IRS990ScheduleD>
